{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-SDK behaviour vectors for the verification primitives. Crypto-free: every",
    "case is a pure input -> outcome mapping, so all four SDKs can assert it from one",
    "file without key material. Loaded by Go, Java, Python and TypeScript unit suites.",
    "",
    "Each SDK's loader asserts the counts below, so adding a case means updating all",
    "four in lockstep - which is the point. To add one, append here and bump the count.",
    "",
    "memo_key covers the governance verification memo, whose key decides whether ECDSA",
    "runs at all. It MUST be injective: an unprefixed concatenation leaves the boundary",
    "between the container and the signature list uncommitted, so a response-controlling",
    "attacker can shift bytes across it and make a MODIFIED container inherit a genuine",
    "one's \"already verified\" status. Each pair is {a, b, expect: distinct|same}.",
    "",
    "",
    "legacy_hash covers WHICH PAYLOAD step 6 must parse. The legacy strips are not injective, so a",
    "server can append a member the strip removes to a genuinely signed payload: the residue is the",
    "signed bytes, every signature check passes, and parsing the DELIVERED payload then returns the",
    "appended value as verified. Each case gives the payload a signer covered and the payload the",
    "server delivered; the SDK must report which variant matched and hand back the covered bytes.",
    "",
    "rule_tier_candidates covers rule selection when the signed payload omits `network` (the common",
    "case, since includeNetworkInPayload has no proto backing and so is never signed). The unsigned",
    "DTO network must not be able to pick a weaker quorum, so every reachable tier is enforced.",
    "See docs/INTEGRITY_VERIFICATION.md for what each primitive is for."
  ],
  "counts": {
